⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
389 calories 41g protein (for the entire pint, mix-ins included)

Peanut Butter Half Baked Protein Ice Cream 😋🍦

Original recipe from my Recipe Book

Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Book with over 150 recipes like this one!

- 400g Fat Free High Protein Milk
- 40-45g sweetener
- 8g (½ tbsp) Peanut Butter
- 16g (2 tbsp) PB Fit
- 1g (¼ tsp) salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) @bobsredmill xanthan gum
Mix-ins:
- 20g of the @fuulsnacks Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough bites
- ⅓ of a @alphaprimebites Protein Brownie
389 cal 35g C, 11g F, 41g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Chop Mix-ins into desired size pieces and freeze for about 1 hour
3. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
4. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
5. Respin if very powdery
6. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with 3/4 of the chopped chopped cookie dough and brownie pieces
7. Run the “Mix-in” cycle
8. Top with the remaining cookie dough and brownie pieces

